course: dictionary
lesson: 8205
title: Reticulate: a net-like pattern
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from science, and they describe something you can see. Reticulate is one of them. It means having a pattern of lines that cross each other, like a net.
explain: Look at an oak leaf. Its veins branch and cross, making a net shape. Grass leaves are different: their veins run side by side, like lines on paper. Scientists call the net pattern reticulate venation.
explain: Use the context. In «the reticulated python», the snake's skin has a net-like pattern. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Net-like fits, so your meaning is right.
explain: Reticulate can also be a verb, but this is rare. To reticulate is to divide or mark something into a network. You will mostly meet it as an adjective in science books.
fact: Reticulate means having a pattern of lines crossing each other like a net.
fact: «Reticulate venation» means the veins in a leaf form a net shape.
fact: Grass leaves have parallel veins, running side by side, not a net.
fact: «The reticulated python» is named for the net-like pattern on its skin.
fact: The reticulated python lives in Southeast Asia, and it can grow over 6 metres long.
exercise: «Oak and rose leaves have reticulate venation.» What does reticulate describe here? | Veins that run side by side | *Veins that cross like a net | Leaves that are very small | Leaves that are shiny
exercise: Grass leaves have parallel veins. Which leaf has reticulate veins? | A straight pine needle | Blade of wheat | *An oak leaf | Grass
exercise: A pupil says reticulate means long. What clue shows the pattern is the real meaning? | Pythons squeeze their prey | Snakes are long | Threadsnakes are small | *Net-like patterns on the skin
test: «Reticulate venation» in a leaf means the veins form what shape? | *A net | A star | A circle | A straight line
test: In «the reticulated python», what does reticulated describe? | Its size only | Its colour only | *Its net-like pattern | Its speed
exam: What does reticulate mean in «The leaf's veins reticulate across its surface»? | Turn yellow | *Form a net-like network across | Grow very fast | Fall off
